  "verbalization": "Marsdenoside K appears to have a shared target relationship with SNU-387 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Marsdenoside K acts as a target for multiple entities, including MOVP-3 and Carboxylesterase 2, which in turn are targets of a common compound, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is ultimately linked to SNU-387, indicating a potential pathway where Marsdenoside K modulates the activity of this compound, which then affects SNU-387. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Marsdenoside K influences the function of a downstream target, which in turn impacts SNU-387. The evidence supports a role for Marsdenoside K in modulating the activity of a shared intermediate, which is critical for the interaction with SNU-387. This suggests that Marsdenoside K may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, with SNU-387 being a downstream effector in this cascade.",
